bagh_palace,_Indore.jpg"}},{"id":"indore_krishnapura_chhatri","areaId":"indore","name":"Krishnapura Chhatri","category":"monument","tags":["history","photo"],"location":{"lat":22.71864,"lng":75.858},"visitMinutes":30,"priceLevel":0,"photoSeed":"indore_krishnapura_chhatri","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsDepicts":0,"commonsNearby":4,"wikiPageviews":274,"wikidataSitelinks":2,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-21"},"hashtags":["krishnapurachhatri","indore"],"bestLight":"morning","summary":"The Krishnapura Chhatris, also known as the Krishna Pura Chhatris are three chhatris located in Indore, Madhya Pradesh, India. The structures were built by the Holkars as cenotaphs over the spots where people of importance were cremated, leading to them also being known as the Holkar Chhatris.","summarySource":"wikipedia","wikipediaTitle":"Krishnapura Chhatri","photo":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/Indore_Krishnapura_Chhatri.JPG/1280px-Indore_Krishnapura_Chhatri.JPG","thumb":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/Indore_Krishnapura_Chhatri.JPG/500px-Indore_Krishnapura_Chhatri.JPG","w":1200,"h":900,"author":"Abhishek727Abhishek Mishra","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Indore_Krishnapura_Chhatri.JPG"}},{"id":"indore_wv_rajawada","areaId":"indore","name":"Rajawada","category":"landmark","tags":["photo"],"location":{"lat":22.71976,"lng":75.85703},"visitMinutes":60,"priceLevel":1,"photoSeed":"indore_wv_rajawada","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsNearby":4,"wikidataSitelinks":0,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-21"},"hashtags":["rajawada","indore"],"summary":"Synonymous with the heart of Indore city, it stands today as a mute witness to the bygone splendor of the Holkar rulers. This 200-year-old, seven-storey historic palace of the Holkars is built in a mixture of Muslim, Maratha and French styles. The lower three floors are made of stone and the upper floors are made of wood, which made it very vulnerable to destruction by fire. Rajwada was burnt thre","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"Indore","photo":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/Rajwada_Palace%2C_Indore.jpg/1280px-Rajwada_Palace%2C_Indore.jpg","thumb":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/Rajwada_Palace%2C_Indore.jpg/500px-Rajwada_Palace%2C_Indore.jpg","w":1200,"h":826,"author":"Bernard Gagnon","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rajwada_Palace,_Indore.jpg"}},{"id":"indore_wv_ravindra_natay_grah","areaId":"indore","name":"Ravindra Natay Grah","category":"landmark","tags":["photo"],"location":{"lat":22.71957,"lng":75.85773},"visitMinutes":60,"priceLevel":1,"photoSeed":"indore_wv_ravindra_natay_grah","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsNearby":4,"wikidataSitelinks":0,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-21"},"hashtags":["ravindranataygrah","indore"],"summary":"This is one of the examples of a complete makeover. Few years back it was an old and not so good auditorium. After some years it was decide to renovate it with public private partnership. it was then done complete makeover and now it is one of the best auditorium in town with many modern facilities.","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"Indore","photo":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Krishnapura_Chhatri_-_Ganesha.jpg/1280px-Krishnapura_Chhatri_-_Ganesha.jpg","thumb":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Krishnapura_Chhatri_-_Ganesha.jpg/500px-Krishnapura_Chhatri_-_Ganesha.jpg","w":1200,"h":1732,"author":"Bernard Gagnon","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Krishnapura_Chhatri_-_Ganesha.jpg"}},{"id":"indore_wv_meghdoot_uapvan","areaId":"indore","name":"Meghdoot Uapvan","category":"park","tags":["nature","photo"],"loc