author":"Bernard Gagnon","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Krishnapura_Chhatri_-_Ganesha.jpg"}},{"id":"indore_wv_shell_city_water_park","areaId":"indore","name":"Shell City Water Park","category":"park","tags":["nature","photo"],"location":{"lat":22.71957,"lng":75.85773},"visitMinutes":60,"priceLevel":0,"photoSeed":"indore_wv_shell_city_water_park","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsNearby":4,"wikidataSitelinks":0,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-21"},"hashtags":["shellcitywaterpark","indore"],"bestLight":"golden","summary":"Another famous water cum amusement park in the outskirts of the busy town. A park that offers wide range of entertainment.","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"Indore","photo":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Krishnapura_Chhatri_-_Ganesha.jpg/1280px-Krishnapura_Chhatri_-_Ganesha.jpg","thumb":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Krishnapura_Chhatri_-_Ganesha.jpg/500px-Krishnapura_Chhatri_-_Ganesha.jpg","w":1200,"h":1732,"author":"Bernard Gagnon","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Krishnapura_Chhatri_-_Ganesha.jpg"}},{"id":"indore_wv_annapurna_temple","areaId":"indore","name":"Annapurna Temple","category":"landmark","tags":["photo"],"location":{"lat":22.72119,"lng":75.90528},"visitMinutes":60,"priceLevel":1,"photoSeed":"indore_wv_annapurna_temple","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsNearby":0,"wikidataSitelinks":0,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-21"},"hashtags":["annapurnatemple","indore"],"summary":"It is a famous temple of the goddess of food. The name of the temple Annapurna means \"anna\" which literally means food. The people in town have great faith in the temple. The temple is made with beautiful colourful work done at the entrance gate.","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"Indore"},{"id":"indore_wv_bada_ganpati","areaId":"indore","name":"Bada Ganpati","category":"landmark","tags":["photo"],"location":{"lat":22.72018,"lng":75.84141},"visitMinutes":60,"priceLevel":1,"photoSeed":"indore_wv_bada_ganpati","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsNearby":0,"wikidataSitelinks":0,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-21"},"hashtags":["badaganpati","indore"],"summary":"Better known for its size than antiquity, this temple houses perhaps the largest Ganesh idol in the world measuring 25 feet from crown to foot. Created as a result of the dream of an Avantika (Ujjain) resident, Shri Dadhich, it was built in 1875.","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"Indore"},{"id":"indore_wv_geeta_bhawan","areaId":"indore","name":"Geeta Bhawan","category":"landmark","tags":["photo"],"location":{"lat":22.71871,"lng":75.88827},"visitMinutes":60,"priceLevel":1,"photoSeed":"indore_wv_geeta_bhawan","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsNearby":0,"wikidataSitelinks":0,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-21"},"hashtags":["geetabhawan","indore"],"summary":"One of the most famous temples in the city. Located near the heart of town (Palasia). You can find idols of almost all gods and goddesses and the peace found here is unique.","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"Indore"},{"id":"indore_wv_gomatgiri","areaId":"indore","name":"Gomatgiri","category":"landmark","tags":["photo"],"location":{"lat":22.74554,"lng":75.7733},"visitMinutes":60,"priceLevel":1,"photoSeed":"indore_wv_gomatgiri","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsNearby":0,"wikidataSitelinks":0,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-21"},"hashtags":["gomatgiri","indore"],"summary":"On the hill 10-12 km away from the heart of the city, the Jain Samaj has constructed a 21-foot statue of Lord Gomateshwar, a replica of the Bahubali statue of Shravanbelagola. Also built here are 24 marble temples with shilars for each tirthankar. This place offers a breathtaking view of Indore city by night.","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"Indore"},{"id":"indore_wv_khajrana_ganesh_temple","areaId":"indore","name":"Khajrana Ganesh Temple","category":"landmark","tags":["photo"],"location":{"lat":22.7303,"lng":75.90797},"visitMinutes":60,"priceLevel":1,"photoSeed":"indore_wv_khajrana_ganesh_temple","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsNearby":0,"wikidataSitelinks":0,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-21"},"hashtags":["khajranaganeshtemple","indore"],"summary":"The citizens of Indore have great faith in this Ganesh temple, built during the reign of Ahilyabai Holkar. It is believed that all wishes are fulfilled by praying here. Nearby is the dargah of Nahar Sayed. This is an important pilgrimage place for Maita Muslims.","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"Indore"},{"id":"indore_wv_venkatesh_temple","areaId":"indore","name":"Venkatesh Temple","category":"landmark","tags":["photo"],"location":{"lat":22.71147,"lng":75.85094},"visitMinutes":60,"priceLevel":1,"photoSeed":"indore_wv_venkatesh_temple","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsNearby":0,"wikidataSitelinks":0,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-21"},"hashtags":["venkateshtemple","indore"],"summary":"Where India's third largest and largest Rath-yatra procession is carried and thousands of people participate in that and temple was built 50 years before in mid of Indore city by Nagoriya Pithdishwar","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"Indore"}],"sources":["Wikidata (CC0)","Wikimedia Commons (counts; photos credited per file)","Wikipedia (pageviews; summaries CC BY-SA 4.0)","Wikivoyage (listings: hours, prices, descriptions; CC BY-SA 4.0)","OpenStreetMap contributors (ODbL): opening hours, fees, websites"]}